{"name":"Rainy Lake","hex":"#3f6c8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rainy Lake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A freshwater lake that straddles the border between Minnesota in the United States and Ontario in Canada.","An unorganized territory in Koochiching County, Minnesota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rainy_Lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rainy Lake","blocks":[{"text":"Rainy Lake is a freshwater lake with a surface area of 930 km2 (360 sq mi) that straddles the border between the United States and Canada. The Rainy River issues from the west side of the lake. Today it is harnessed to make hydroelectricity for United States (US) and Canadian locations. International Falls, Minnesota and the much smaller city of Ranier, Minnesota are situated opposite Fort Frances, Ontario, on either side of the Rainy River. Rainy Lake and Rainy River establish part of the boundary between the U.S. state of Minnesota and the Canadian province of Ontario."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Rainy_Lake_from_Tango_Channel.jpg/330px-Rainy_Lake_from_Tango_Channel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainy_Lake","wikidata":"Q202019"},{"title":"Rainy Lake (Moira drainage basin)","blocks":[{"text":"Rainy Lake is a lake in the Moira River and Lake Ontario drainage basins in Addington Highlands, Lennox and Addington County, Ontario, Canada."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainy_Lake_(Moira_drainage_basin)","wikidata":"Q7285006"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain","wikidata":"Q7925"},{"title":"Lake","blocks":[{"text":"A lake is often a naturally occurring, relatively large and fixed body of water on or near the Earth's surface. It is localized in a basin or interconnected basins surrounded by dry land. Lakes lie completely on land and are separate from the ocean, although they may be connected with the ocean by outflowing rivers. Lakes, like other bodies of water, are part of the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Most lakes are fresh water and account for almost all the world's surface freshwater, but some are salt lakes with salinities even higher than that of seawater. Lakes vary significantly in surface area and volume of water, but in total cover approximately 2.5 × 106 km2 (less than 2%) of the Earth's surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg/330px-Lake_Idro_Italy_2005-08-16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake","wikidata":"Q23397"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/500px-Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/1280px-Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg/500px-Rainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainy_Lake_by_Sentinel-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg/500px-Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg/1280px-Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg/500px-Rainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rocky shoreline on Rainy Lake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainy_Lake_Shoreline.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/A555%2C_Voyageurs_National_Park%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%2C_2013.jpg/500px-A555%2C_Voyageurs_National_Park%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/A555%2C_Voyageurs_National_Park%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%2C_2013.jpg/500px-A555%2C_Voyageurs_National_Park%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%2C_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ice road in April 2013","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA555%2C_Voyageurs_National_Park%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%2C_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Mermaid_Sculpture_on_Rainy_Lake.jpg/500px-Mermaid_Sculpture_on_Rainy_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Mer